[[:db/retract 17592186185700 :answer-field/choices 17592186185701] [:db/retract 17592186185700 :answer-field/choices 17592186185702] [:db/retract 17592186185700 :answer-field/choices 17592186185703] [:db/retract 17592186185700 :answer-field/choices 17592186185704] [:db/retract 17592186185700 :answer-field/choices 17592186185705] {:db/id 17592186188300 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1226ca92-65ae-56a2-b931-338a3cdb6d88" "question-35514c08-5e3f-5179-9038-1219b52d39dc" "question-9fc21508-9f85-5150-8047-4615f447db2e" "question-230a08c0-5208-5936-927a-cc4ab89b2be1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188007 :question/problem "Suppose we want to measure the volume of a shoe box. What units could we use?\n\nI. $\\textrm{cm}^2$\n\nII. $\\textrm{cm}^3$\n\nIII. $\\textrm{kg}$" :question/worked-solution "We can measure length in centimeters $(\\textrm{cm}).$ When measuring lengths in centimeters, volumes are measured in $\\textrm{cm} \\times \\textrm{cm} \\times \\textrm{cm},$ which is usually written as $\\textrm{cm}^3.$ \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188302 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bbbe35dd-2bbc-5214-98a6-eb9aaf15d8bf" "question-92a736d5-f3b8-5c3c-b7af-b2d6520c2b8f" "question-bf19de17-406e-5637-9313-1be02592e867" "question-44b69e39-7dc4-5902-a9e6-91ffdc7daa00"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188009 :question/problem "![](images/7e/7e300a90dbfda5a9210cec502c2879b7950e2765c433eb6ee6284e74db3cd220.png)\n\n What is the area of the square above?" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(5\\,\\text{ft})^{2} \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{ft}\\times 5\\,\\text{ft} \\\\  & =(5\\times 5)\\times (\\text{ft}\\times \\text{ft}) \\\\  & =25\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188008 :question/proble